        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug is caused by the potential for a deadlock in the `runCommand` method of the `Shell` class, specifically when managing the error stream thread (`errThread`). If the `errThread` does not exit properly because it is not joined correctly, it can lead to the main process waiting indefinitely, resulting in a deadlock situation. This issue arises from the previous handling of `InterruptedException` during thread joining, which could leave the `errThread` still alive and waiting on resources that are no longer available.

        Commit message:
        HADOOP-10622. Shell.runCommand can deadlock. Contributed by
 Gera Shegalov

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/hadoop/common/trunk@1602033 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68  

